Subject: memory-setting: a Memory setting (DM_MEMORY_GB: auto, or a number of
 GB) says how much of the Mac the game plans for

Ported from Fasen24-AI/swordboiMacNative 790245d6 and d343de61 (EmmanueleC, MIT) onto nxnative bee218d9.
rule_ws() is Metal's working set, or that of a device with the memory the player names (0.74 of it), when that
is less. It moves where the GPU memory guard begins to let go (guard_init), how many textures are made ahead of
their first read (pool_budget) and from when NXForge's read marks age (seen_cap_kb). Where the guard stops the
game stays the device's own limit. The fork's other reader, the takeover's hold of compressible sharing entries,
is gone from nvn_mtl.m (nxnative's nvn_owner.m now owns the sharing table). settings.tsv: a Memory choice row in
Performance for NVN games.
